Chapter: SixlowpanEncodeTest

  cites Encode chapter Sixlowpan

 Exercise 6LoWPAN: the IPHC base-header flag encoding and the FRAG1 /
 FRAGN fragmentation headers. Byte sequences checked against the RFC
 6282 / 4944 bit layout. opening returns the count of passing checks.

Section: Helpers

  bytes-eq : List Integer, List Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq (a) (b) =
   if list-length a /= list-length b then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b 0 (list-length a)

  bytes-eq-loop : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  bytes-eq-loop (a) (b) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then True
   else if list-at a i /= list-at b i then False
   else bytes-eq-loop a b (i + 1) len

  flag : Boolean -> Integer
  flag (b) = if b then 1 else 0

Section: Checks

 IPHC with TF elided (3), NH inline (0), HLIM 64 (2), source and
 destination address mode 16-bit (1): base header 0x7A 0x11.

  check-iphc : Integer
  check-iphc =
   flag (bytes-eq (lowpan-iphc 3 0 2 0 0 1 0 0 1) [122, 17])

  check-frag1 : Integer
  check-frag1 =
   flag (bytes-eq (lowpan-frag1 1280 #00AB) [197, 0, 0, 171])

  check-fragn : Integer
  check-fragn =
   flag (bytes-eq (lowpan-fragn 1280 #00AB 16) [229, 0, 0, 171, 16])

  check-dispatch : Integer
  check-dispatch =
   flag (if lowpan-dispatch-frag1 == 192 then lowpan-dispatch-fragn == 224 else False)

  opening : Integer =
   let a = check-iphc
   in let b = check-frag1
   in let c = check-fragn
   in let d = check-dispatch
   in a + b + c + d
